      "physical_description": null,
      "summary": "Woman’s wrapper composed of 18 hand woven strips of handspun cotton, hand sewn together along the selvedges (aso oke). The strips have a uniform pattern. The warp has a central stripe of red magenta alaari silk, flanked by two bands of white cotton of equal width; in 17 of the strips the alaari is only a narrow stripe, but in the central strip it is as wide as the flanking bands of white. The weft is of white alternating with a single shade indigo to produce a weft pattern of a band of indigo flanked by two thin lines. The outermost strip has an extension at one end that serves as a tie. The warp ends have not been hemmed.",
